>Check that the script sets up the HACKDIR env var to point to the
>nethack playground dir. (or, if you run nethack directly, that you
>set HACKDIR yourself)

Also, be sure that /usr/games/lib/nethackdir and any subdirectories has group
games, and is writeable by the group:

drwxrwxr-x   1 games   games   4096  2003-12-08 00:48 nethackdir

These commands should set things up correctly, if run as root:

chown -R games:games /usr/games/lib/nethackdir
chmod g+x games /usr/games/lib/nethackdir/nethack
find /usr/games/lib/nethackdir -type d | xargs chmod 0775

The chown command resets any setuid or setgid bits, so you'll need to use the
first chmod command even if these bits were previously set.



